      "body": "Upon further investigation, I think I have identified the issue.\n\nDuring the collection of the tests, when `nodeid` is being calculated, if the path to the test is outside of the `config.rootpath`, then paths to the tests' locations given as CLI argument are used for `nodeid` calculation.\nThis happens [here](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/9cf2cae94355cd83ad7e8d88f976c5a524c98cfb/src/_pytest/nodes.py#L597)\n\nHowever, later, when the terminal output is being created ([here](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/9cf2cae94355cd83ad7e8d88f976c5a524c98cfb/src/_pytest/config/__init__.py#L1186)), nodeid is joined with `config.rootpath`, resulting in the invalid path seen in the output.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
